1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,297
This sink base came out well. Let’s keep it in the Library for the next kitchen.

2
00:00:07,297 --> 00:00:25,203
Save as template copies the whole cabinet: sizes, materials, construction and hardware.

3
00:00:25,203 --> 00:00:32,721
The Library is shared by every job: templates, sheet materials, edgebands and hardware.

4
00:00:32,721 --> 00:00:36,751
Edit a template in the same cabinet editor. Existing jobs keep their own copy.

5
00:00:36,751 --> 00:00:48,848
Set it to the shop standard: 34-1/2" high and 23-1/4" deep.

6
00:00:48,848 --> 00:00:53,155
Materials: code, thickness and sheet size drive the parts and the nesting.

7
00:00:53,155 --> 00:01:05,899
Add a price so costs show up. Until then a Configure badge marks it as not set.

8
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:10,620
Edgebands: the tapes your edgebander runs, by code.

9
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:17,884
Hardware: Salice hinges and plates, Blum TANDEM slides, dowels and screws.

10
00:01:17,884 --> 00:01:25,399
Each item keeps the numbers the drilling uses, like the hinge cup size and depth.

11
00:01:25,399 --> 00:01:32,462
Drilling patterns: the hole layouts, checked against the Salice and Blum sheets.

12
00:01:32,462 --> 00:01:40,436
Each one shows where the numbers came from, with a link to the maker’s sheet.

13
00:01:40,436 --> 00:01:46,155
Machining rules turn layer names in imported drawings into drill, pocket and cut steps.
